# AngularJS Client

## Module and routing

- Root module: `goldPointsApp`. Feature modules extend it (e.g. `goldPointsApp.auth`, `goldPointsApp.admin`).
- Routes via ui-router `$stateProvider` in feature `*.js` files.
- HTML5 mode enabled — use ui-sref, not hash URLs.

## Component pattern

Newer features use ES6 classes registered as components:

```javascript
class MainController {
  constructor($http, Auth, User) { /* inject deps */ }
  $onInit() { /* load data */ }
}
angular.module('goldPointsApp').component('main', {
  templateUrl: 'app/main/main.html',
  controller: MainController
});
```

## Templates and data

- Colocate `*.html`, `*.css`, `*.js` per feature under `client/app/<feature>/`.
- `$http` calls hit `/api/*` endpoints.
- Auth: `Auth.isLoggedIn()`, `Auth.hasRole()`, `Auth.isAdmin()` from `client/components/auth/`.
- Guest users auto-query by email on main page load.
- Use ui-select, toaster notifications, and Bootstrap classes for layout.

## Do not

- Introduce React, Vue, or Angular 2+ patterns.
- Add TypeScript or modern build tooling unless explicitly requested.
